WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.393 --> 00:00:11.226
- [Interviewer] All right, Ke'.

00:00:11.226 --> 00:00:12.059
Ke' where'd you grow up?

00:00:12.059 --> 00:00:13.660
Where are you from originally?

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:16.650
- I grew up in Inglewood, California.

00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.790
- [Interviewer] And tell
me about your childhood,

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.324
you had both your parents growing up?

00:00:20.324 --> 00:00:24.010
- No, my father was arrested due

00:00:24.010 --> 00:00:27.380
to murder when I was like 2 years old

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:29.540
and my mom got caught
up in the street life,

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:31.310
when I was around 5.

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.340
- [Interviewer] And who raised you?

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.312
- My grandmother.

00:00:33.312 --> 00:00:34.145
- [Interviewer] Grandmother.

00:00:34.145 --> 00:00:34.978
- Hmm.

00:00:34.978 --> 00:00:37.600
- [Interviewer] How was
your childhood after all?

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.720
- It was pretty difficult
because I seen all the kids going

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.300
to school with parents
and I didn't have either.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:44.550
All I had was my grandmother.

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.623
And later on down the line,
I ended up losing her.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.200
So everything that seemed
like everything to me,

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.150
got taken away.

00:00:53.150 --> 00:00:53.983
- [Interviewer] At what age?

00:00:53.983 --> 00:00:54.890
- 12.

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:56.610
- [Interviewer] So from
12 on where'd you go?

00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:57.720
- I had to grow up pretty fast.

00:00:57.720 --> 00:00:59.410
I went with my other grandmother,

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:01.780
which there was always a question

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:04.090
as if I belong to this family or not.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.150
And it was kind of hurtful

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.300
'cause I felt like the
black sheep of the family.

00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.050
So I got pushed away from them too.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.130
And I ended up doing a lot
of crazy things in life.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.640
I started prostituting, selling drugs.

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.350
I had kids at a very young age.

00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:23.723
- [Interviewer] Where did
you start working the street?

00:01:23.723 --> 00:01:27.347
- I actually started
working on Fig in 95th.

00:01:27.347 --> 00:01:28.430
- [Interviewer] At what age?

00:01:28.430 --> 00:01:29.604
- At 18.

00:01:29.604 --> 00:01:31.845
- [Interviewer] 18?

00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:35.080
- Yes, 18 Fig in 95th was the first street

00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:36.490
I ever got down on.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:40.520
It was one of the most
terrifying nights of my life.

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.460
I was told all these things
to do and what not to do.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.670
And I was so scared.

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:47.050
I don't know what to do if
somebody might kidnap me,

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:50.570
kill me, but I ran with it ,because it was

00:01:50.570 --> 00:01:53.043
the only way that I could
find a source of income.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.150
- [Interviewer] Did you have a pimp?

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:56.496
- Yes, I did.

00:01:56.496 --> 00:01:58.333
- [Interviewer] How did he treat you?

00:01:58.333 --> 00:02:01.370
- Actually, every guy that I've dealt

00:02:02.663 --> 00:02:06.400
with in that line of work, were more so

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:10.090
in love with me versus trying to pit me.

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:13.640
So it was, I did it by choice

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:15.253
but not because he forced me to.

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:17.630
And any man that I dealt

00:02:17.630 --> 00:02:21.150
with in that field had their own hustle,

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:23.341
meaning they were drug dealers

00:02:23.341 --> 00:02:27.200
or had jobs to where it was both 50-50.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:29.240
We both bringing something to the table,

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.550
but I had my fair share

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:34.480
off some that were kind of
crazy, that were abusive.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:35.910
That took all my money.

00:02:35.910 --> 00:02:38.610
That would leave me out all night.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.950
And they went and just
spent money on cars, chains,

00:02:41.950 --> 00:02:43.513
and other women.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:48.100
While I worked hard for
it, it was pretty painful,

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:50.650
but eventually you grow after it.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.093
You learn what to do and what not to do.

00:02:52.093 --> 00:02:53.570
- [Interviewer] So back
to that first night

00:02:53.570 --> 00:02:55.453
that you were working in the street.

00:02:55.453 --> 00:02:56.286
- Hmmm.

00:02:56.286 --> 00:02:57.380
- [Interviewer] Do you
remember that night?

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:58.213
- Yes, I do,

00:02:58.213 --> 00:03:00.233
I remember it as if
just happened yesterday,

00:03:03.112 --> 00:03:08.010
the guy we ended up meeting
each other that night

00:03:08.010 --> 00:03:10.750
and I thought he wanted
to be my boyfriend, right?

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.560
So I went and I chill with
him at his family's house.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.060
And he was like, "Have you
ever sold that before?"

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:18.260
And I was like, "What
do you mean by that?"

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:20.960
He was like, you know, "Like
you could get paid for it

00:03:22.087 --> 00:03:24.707
"but let me test the product
first to see (Laughing)

00:03:24.707 --> 00:03:25.960
"how much it's worth."

00:03:25.960 --> 00:03:27.840
And I'm thinking he's joking, right?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.407
So we messing around and then he's like,

00:03:29.407 --> 00:03:32.207
"All right, seriously, we
(indistinct) go to Fig right now."

00:03:33.618 --> 00:03:36.477
And I was like, "Okay, well call me crazy.

00:03:36.477 --> 00:03:38.367
"I thought it was better.

00:03:38.367 --> 00:03:40.157
"I'm out here messing
around with me and for free

00:03:40.157 --> 00:03:42.190
"why not get a dollar for it?"

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:43.023
So he told me,

00:03:43.023 --> 00:03:45.147
"Okay you're not supposed
to date black people,

00:03:45.147 --> 00:03:46.407
"you're not supposed to get in cars

00:03:46.407 --> 00:03:47.577
"with these license plates,

00:03:47.577 --> 00:03:48.410
"you're not supposed to do this,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.243
"not supposed to"

00:03:49.243 --> 00:03:50.530
He gave me a whole rundown.

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:52.980
And I'm like sheep, wow.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:54.610
First mistake I made was jumping

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.559
in the car with a black man.

00:03:56.559 --> 00:03:58.010
(Laughing)

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.783
And I found out the reason was

00:03:59.783 --> 00:04:02.670
because 9 times out of
10 they're pimps, right?

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:06.780
So, I jumped in the car,
every dollar that I made

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.870
it's just rules to this game.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.320
So every dollar that I
made, he took my money,

00:04:12.320 --> 00:04:13.620
he took my cell phone,

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.170
he called the dude that I was
messing with, let them know.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.460
Yeah, she was out of pocket.

00:04:17.460 --> 00:04:19.230
I'm taking everything.

00:04:19.230 --> 00:04:21.060
And she got to pay me.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.519
I was like, "Damn, this
is how this works."

00:04:23.519 --> 00:04:24.352
(Laughing)

00:04:24.352 --> 00:04:26.630
Like I have no say in none of it.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.830
I just went with it.

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.110
Eventually, the more I stayed in the game

00:04:30.110 --> 00:04:32.710
the more I got more of the game

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.250
and I was able to start doing things

00:04:34.250 --> 00:04:38.196
on my own and it made
my game a lot tighter.

00:04:38.196 --> 00:04:40.720
And it made me a lot wiser listening

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:43.950
to other females stories,

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:45.850
and the things that they been through.

00:04:47.030 --> 00:04:48.330
It kinda made me stronger.

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:50.800
- [Interviewer] Had you
been arrested for it?

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.240
- Yes, Lynwood knows me personally.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:55.073
- [Interviewer] I'm sorry.

00:04:55.073 --> 00:04:58.133
- I said Lynwood County
Jail knows me personally.

00:04:59.350 --> 00:05:00.183
(Laughing)

00:05:00.183 --> 00:05:02.423
Which is sad and unfortunate, but yes.

00:05:02.423 --> 00:05:04.660
- [Interviewer] So how did you
end up down here on Skid Row?

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:06.710
- Ooh, I ended up down here

00:05:06.710 --> 00:05:09.603
on Skid Row because I
had hit my rock bottom.

00:05:12.226 --> 00:05:16.917
I was with the love of my life
who had just been arrested,

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:23.220
and not too long before that happened,

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:26.020
I had had all three of my
children taken away from me.

00:05:26.020 --> 00:05:29.270
So I had already felt
like I was a little empty.

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:32.930
So to have the person that
helped me get through this stuff

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.850
get taken away from me.

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.720
It kind tore me down,
which led me to do drugs.

00:05:37.720 --> 00:05:39.380
I was popping ecstasy pills,

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:40.530
I was doing Coke,

00:05:40.530 --> 00:05:41.610
I was doing crystal.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:42.940
The only thing I'm never tried

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:46.130
in this world is heroin
and crack and acid.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.460
But I was doing everything,

00:05:47.460 --> 00:05:50.470
and I ended up losing places.

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:52.120
I had to stay,

00:05:52.120 --> 00:05:53.870
and I ended up coming down here.

00:05:53.870 --> 00:05:56.343
Which I met my mom, which was no help.

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:58.380
'Cause every time like,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:02.050
I mean she'll throw a dollar
or 2 every now and again.

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:04.210
But actually say that she genuinely cares

00:06:04.210 --> 00:06:05.670
they wanna talk to me

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.130
and figure out the things
that I'm going through.

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:09.330
No, I never felt like
she wanted to do that.

00:06:10.737 --> 00:06:15.737
But, I came down here and I
started to get to know people

00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.800
like genuinely caring
about who these people are

00:06:20.445 --> 00:06:21.460
and what do they have to offer.

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:23.800
Because there's a lesson
in everybody that we meet

00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.600
whether you take the lesson
or leave it, it's up to you.

00:06:27.936 --> 00:06:31.290
So I met this guy down here and I met him

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:34.313
through my mother and he was
like a really good friend.

00:06:34.313 --> 00:06:39.313
We connected on levels
that I can't even explain.

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:40.458
Like conversation-wise he never came at me

00:06:40.458 --> 00:06:41.291
disrespectfully, like I really felt

00:06:41.291 --> 00:06:46.291
like it was something special about him.

00:06:48.030 --> 00:06:52.490
So I gave him the time of
day, like just to be friends.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:55.360
And one day we decided
to take that friendship

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:57.060
a little further than what it was.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:07:00.050
And I feel like that was the worst mistake

00:07:00.050 --> 00:07:01.650
that I could have made downtown.

00:07:03.620 --> 00:07:05.413
I got pregnant by this guy.

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:09.340
I started talking to the
love of my life for this guy.

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:15.360
Like, it felt like I could
have a piece of happiness.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:18.000
And if I could have that, I was willing

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:21.613
to let go anything that
would stop it from unfolding.

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.920
So I stopped talking to a lot of men.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:27.890
I stopped talking to the
person who I felt God made

00:07:27.890 --> 00:07:32.060
for me just to see where things
would go with this person.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:33.760
I ended up finding out a couple

00:07:33.760 --> 00:07:35.933
of weeks ago that I was pregnant.

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.660
I told the guy, he said
whatever you decide to do

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:41.510
I got your back, no matter.

00:07:41.510 --> 00:07:43.040
So I decided to keep my child

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:48.960
'cause it's just not something
that I wanted to get rid of.

00:07:49.340 --> 00:07:50.400
I've been through that before

00:07:50.400 --> 00:07:51.700
and it's something very painful

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:54.300
that no woman I feel should
ever have to go through.

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:58.130
So we both decided, "Okay,
this is what we gonna do."

00:07:58.130 --> 00:08:01.707
So he asked me, "well, what
do we need to do to make sure

00:08:01.707 --> 00:08:05.580
"that we don't bring our child
into this world in a tent?".

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:08.890
So we hustled and the
whole time I'm thinking

00:08:08.890 --> 00:08:11.090
we were building this life and we got

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:16.090
these beautiful things, when
unfold and occur in our lives,

00:08:17.270 --> 00:08:19.965
when this whole time I was the only person

00:08:19.965 --> 00:08:23.380
in this relationship, like
I really felt like I had

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:29.270
everything that I wanted
without the value of a dollar.

00:08:29.270 --> 00:08:32.610
And I lived in a tent,
but it was taken from me

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:36.543
because he decided to wanna
mess around with other women.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:41.483
I only found out because of
the fact that he paid my mom.

00:08:42.360 --> 00:08:46.763
Dope, do not say nothing
to me about this woman.

00:08:49.060 --> 00:08:50.160
And it was really painful

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:52.393
because I really gave
my all to this person.

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:56.810
And he just really took my heart

00:08:56.810 --> 00:08:58.257
after me telling him, "If you feel

00:08:58.257 --> 00:09:01.677
"like you're gonna hurt
me, please just walk away."

00:09:03.060 --> 00:09:05.160
And he did not the guts to just walk away.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:10.450
- [Interviewer] And the other gentlemen

00:09:10.450 --> 00:09:11.850
that you were involved with,

00:09:12.818 --> 00:09:13.651
- Yes.

00:09:13.651 --> 00:09:14.750
- What happened with him?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:16.850
- He's actually still in prison right now.

00:09:17.820 --> 00:09:22.820
And I feel so bad because, if
he was free there's nothing

00:09:22.924 --> 00:09:25.723
in this world that I couldn't
have gotten from him.

00:09:26.780 --> 00:09:29.270
And I felt like I turned my back on him

00:09:29.270 --> 00:09:32.880
in the time that he needed
me the most for a piece

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:35.633
of happiness that I would never receive.

00:09:37.410 --> 00:09:39.780
- [Interviewer] So how far
along is your pregnancy?

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:42.050
- I haven't even been to the doctor yet.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:43.670
- [Interviewer] So fairly new.

00:09:43.670 --> 00:09:46.763
- But I can't be no more than two months.

00:09:49.290 --> 00:09:50.833
- [Interviewer] And
what's he in prison for?

00:09:53.850 --> 00:09:54.683
- Possession

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:58.890
- [Interviewer] How old are you?

00:09:58.890 --> 00:09:59.750
- 26.

00:09:59.750 --> 00:10:03.980
- [Interviewer] 26, and
you were working Figueroa

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.280
you did that for how long?

00:10:06.247 --> 00:10:10.010
- Oh, I did it when I
was 18 for about a year,

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.202
then I stopped for six years

00:10:12.202 --> 00:10:13.035
after I had my kids, but then life hit me

00:10:13.035 --> 00:10:18.035
where my 9-5 wasn't supportive enough

00:10:21.340 --> 00:10:22.423
of three kids.

00:10:23.640 --> 00:10:28.287
In the world we live in the
economy is very expensive,

00:10:28.287 --> 00:10:29.760
so wasn't enough.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:31.583
So it led me back to the streets.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:34.780
And I've been in the streets since then.

00:10:36.229 --> 00:10:39.779
- [Interviewer] (Indistinct)

00:10:39.779 --> 00:10:41.550
- Hmm, honestly on a good day.

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:45.900
I'd probably bring like 4 in
the day and maybe 4 at night.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:47.310
If I did a double shift

00:10:48.210 --> 00:10:52.500
or if I just wanted to just
get some stuff out the way

00:10:53.490 --> 00:10:56.483
like four 3 was maybe the
lowest I would ever bring.

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:02.880
- [Interviewer] Ad did you
ever get any bad experiences

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:04.710
with the guys you picked up?

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:05.666
- [Ke'] Very many,

00:11:05.666 --> 00:11:09.020
(indistinct) one in particular.

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:10.800
I had a guy who was pushing his car

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:13.212
in the middle of the streets, right?

00:11:13.212 --> 00:11:14.681
And me I'm just a genuine person,

00:11:14.681 --> 00:11:16.210
I like to see the good

00:11:16.210 --> 00:11:19.900
in everybody just because I like to think

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.630
that everybody has some
type of good in him.

00:11:21.630 --> 00:11:23.740
So he's pushing his car in
the middle of the streets.

00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.737
He's like, "Hey, can you help me?

00:11:25.737 --> 00:11:26.797
"I need you to just push it

00:11:26.797 --> 00:11:28.170
"so I can get a jumpstart."

00:11:28.170 --> 00:11:29.003
So like, "Okay, sure,

00:11:29.003 --> 00:11:31.367
"let's push your car off
the middle of the street

00:11:31.367 --> 00:11:32.980
"so you won't get it hit."

00:11:32.980 --> 00:11:34.240
He would push the car to the side.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.310
He's like, "Okay, well, you
know, I want to date you."

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:38.350
So I get in the car with
him after we get it started

00:11:38.350 --> 00:11:42.123
we pull around the corner
and the guy's like,

00:11:44.775 --> 00:11:48.247
"Okay one rule about the
game that we never do.

00:11:48.247 --> 00:11:53.247
"We don't provide any services
without receiving a dollar."

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:58.040
For some reason, he would
not give me the dollars.

00:11:58.040 --> 00:11:59.237
And I kept telling him, "Okay sir,

00:11:59.237 --> 00:12:00.400
"well I'm not doing anything

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:01.930
unless you give me the dollars."

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:04.310
So he pulls a bottle
from underneath the seat

00:12:04.310 --> 00:12:07.947
and like he's finna crack me
in the head with the bottle,

00:12:07.947 --> 00:12:12.200
"You gonna do this or I'm finna hit you."

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.000
So I had a pepper spray
on the side of my hip

00:12:15.000 --> 00:12:16.190
and I took the pepper spray out.

00:12:16.190 --> 00:12:18.410
This is my first time
ever having experience

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:19.243
with a pepper spray.

00:12:19.243 --> 00:12:20.720
So it was kind of funny.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.580
So I sprayed the pepper spray

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:26.480
not knowing we're in a
car that is sealed off.

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:28.180
I never been around pepper spray before.

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:30.147
So I'm thinking, "Okay,
I spray him in the face

00:12:30.147 --> 00:12:31.470
"he gonna get off of me."

00:12:31.470 --> 00:12:32.880
I sprayed the pepper spray,

00:12:32.880 --> 00:12:34.020
we both started coughing.

00:12:34.020 --> 00:12:34.947
I said, "What the fuck?

00:12:34.947 --> 00:12:36.217
"I didn't get it on me."

00:12:36.217 --> 00:12:38.080
And me my eyes was watering,

00:12:38.080 --> 00:12:39.130
my nose was running.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:41.615
He takes off running
down the street crying.

00:12:41.615 --> 00:12:43.665
He left his car.

00:12:43.665 --> 00:12:46.570
Me I take off running the other way.

00:12:46.570 --> 00:12:48.880
My eyes is just running
,my nose is running.

00:12:48.880 --> 00:12:50.860
I'm looking for anybody for help.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:53.360
Then I run into another
guy he wants to date.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:56.540
But then when we date, I get
the pepper spray on the condom,

00:12:56.540 --> 00:12:57.880
so now I'm burning down here.

00:12:57.880 --> 00:12:59.457
I was like, "Okay, listen, I'm done.

00:12:59.457 --> 00:13:03.288
"I need to go now(indistinct)

00:13:03.288 --> 00:13:04.570
"It's over, it's a wrap."

00:13:04.570 --> 00:13:06.530
That was one of the crazy experiences

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:07.980
I've experienced on Figueroa.

00:13:09.100 --> 00:13:09.933
- [Interviewer] You've ever get raped,

00:13:09.933 --> 00:13:11.067
beaten up stuff like that?

00:13:11.067 --> 00:13:13.020
- No, I've almost got robbed before.

00:13:13.020 --> 00:13:14.060
- [Interviewer] I bet.

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:17.870
- Yeah, no, actually I take
that back when I first started

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:18.760
in 2012, there was this
guy out here, right?

00:13:18.760 --> 00:13:21.410
He would run around

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.590
and pretend like he was a police officer.

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:25.150
And I do believe I seen on the news,

00:13:25.150 --> 00:13:27.570
he got arrested, but he
would go around and pretend

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:30.180
like he was a police officer,
making girls do things.

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:31.763
Oh, I know you got warrants.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.257
And so he would make them create

00:13:35.257 --> 00:13:38.647
ex he did it to me before,
"Oh, come with me."

00:13:39.720 --> 00:13:41.550
I never done any of day in my life.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.860
But that day that man made me do it.

00:13:43.860 --> 00:13:46.950
Because I was so in fear
that I was gonna go to jail.

00:13:46.950 --> 00:13:48.387
He's like, "I'm gonna give you a pass,

00:13:48.387 --> 00:13:50.930
"if we go around the corner, we do this."

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:52.193
I cried the whole time.

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:55.170
And eventually he let me go.

00:13:55.170 --> 00:13:58.500
I seen him driving down
the street a couple

00:13:58.500 --> 00:14:00.100
of weeks later and he
told me to get in the car.

00:14:00.100 --> 00:14:03.600
He said, anytime I come and
get you just get in the car

00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:05.150
and you won't go to jail.

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:07.000
I'll let them know not to bother you.

00:14:09.345 --> 00:14:13.187
Eventually a woman found
out that it was a fake

00:14:14.440 --> 00:14:16.800
and she told, and that man was arrested.

00:14:16.800 --> 00:14:20.913
I seen it on the news after
I had left that lifestyle.

00:14:21.900 --> 00:14:24.620
And it made me feel so
good because it's like

00:14:24.620 --> 00:14:29.180
it's already a burden on us
as women that we have do this.

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:33.300
And then the fact that
people judge and look

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:36.120
at us a certain type of
way, because of the hustle

00:14:36.120 --> 00:14:38.030
that we have, it's kinda hard.

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:39.460
It's kinda really messed up,

00:14:39.460 --> 00:14:42.120
'cause you don't know why we ended up here

00:14:42.120 --> 00:14:44.890
or what we're doing what
the purposes is for,

00:14:44.890 --> 00:14:48.330
is not because we like
it or because we love it.

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:50.893
Maybe is the only source
of income that we know of.

00:14:53.170 --> 00:14:56.457
But a lot of people take
that as an advantage.

00:14:56.457 --> 00:14:57.887
"Oh, they're just whores,

00:14:58.737 --> 00:15:01.657
"they have no respect, we don't need

00:15:01.657 --> 00:15:02.980
"to show them any respect."

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:04.730
We don't need to show them any type

00:15:05.608 --> 00:15:07.903
of like respectful conversation.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:12.680
That's not cool, 'cause
at the end of the day,

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.190
we're still human beings.

00:15:15.190 --> 00:15:18.100
Whether we decide to
hustle with the rock side

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:22.800
or with the gifts and the abilities

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:24.570
that God blessed us with,

00:15:24.570 --> 00:15:26.893
we have to survive just
like everybody else.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.050
- [Interviewer] Was
giving up their lifestyle

00:15:29.050 --> 00:15:31.447
what brought you down to Skid Row?

00:15:31.447 --> 00:15:34.470
- Yes, when I left the lifestyle,

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.489
I ended up on Skid Row

00:15:36.489 --> 00:15:37.660
because I can't tolerate no more.

00:15:37.660 --> 00:15:39.630
- [Interviewer] So you went
from South Central to Skid Row?

00:15:39.630 --> 00:15:40.463
- Yes.

00:15:40.463 --> 00:15:41.550
- [Interviewer] Which is a big step down.

00:15:41.550 --> 00:15:43.349
- Yes, a huge step down

00:15:43.349 --> 00:15:44.520
(Laughing)

00:15:44.520 --> 00:15:46.210
this I tell people all the time,

00:15:46.210 --> 00:15:47.770
I'm bougie ghetto, these (indistinct).

00:15:47.770 --> 00:15:51.524
I never knew of like, when
I first got down here...

00:15:51.524 --> 00:15:53.480
- [Interviewer] There's
no tents down (indistinct)

00:15:53.480 --> 00:15:55.870
- There's no tents ,South central

00:15:55.870 --> 00:15:58.910
the first day I got down
here, I see my mom in a tent.

00:15:58.910 --> 00:15:59.930
I see a bed,

00:15:59.930 --> 00:16:01.020
I see everything else.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:03.290
I said, "What the fuck?

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:05.447
'Why are you so comfortable in this tent?

00:16:05.447 --> 00:16:09.632
And it took for me to have to
go through it, to understand.

00:16:09.632 --> 00:16:10.465
- [Interviewer] There are thing people

00:16:10.465 --> 00:16:11.580
that watch my channel don't

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:12.413
understand the difference

00:16:12.413 --> 00:16:13.740
between South Central and Skid Row.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:14.870
They think there're similar

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.080
