00:17:18.464 --> 00:17:19.297
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:17:19.297 --> 00:17:20.897
- Is a huge difference.

00:17:20.897 --> 00:17:21.840
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.913
- And is sad because it's
like, these are humans too.

00:17:28.816 --> 00:17:30.895
- [Interviewer] When you were
a kid, did you have dreams

00:17:30.895 --> 00:17:34.147
of doing something with
your life other than this?

00:17:35.294 --> 00:17:40.294
- Yes, I've always had a dream
of owning my own hair salon

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:42.863
but having like a little twist to it.

00:17:44.400 --> 00:17:46.850
I wanted to call it a piece

00:17:46.850 --> 00:17:49.883
of quiet that a parent can't find.

00:17:50.870 --> 00:17:51.905
'Cause we have a lot of
single parents out here

00:17:51.905 --> 00:17:56.905
that can't like really do things

00:17:57.380 --> 00:18:00.150
for themselves because they
always have their children

00:18:00.150 --> 00:18:02.060
or they don't have time
for a sitter or anything.

00:18:02.060 --> 00:18:04.190
So I wanted to create this business

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:07.190
to where people can come and still unwind

00:18:07.190 --> 00:18:10.980
and have that quiet time
that they need as adults

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:13.580
while their children are
downstairs being cared for.

00:18:14.870 --> 00:18:17.070
So a peace of mind that
a parent can't find.

00:18:18.880 --> 00:18:19.770
- [Interviewer] Do you
feel like all these years

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:22.120
on the street has changed you somehow?

00:18:22.120 --> 00:18:24.620
- Yes, has made me a lot
stronger and a lot wiser.

00:18:27.348 --> 00:18:31.283
Without the streets, I
probably wouldn't be here.

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:35.170
I've met a lot of mothers in the streets

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:39.280
and what I mean by that is a
woman that I never even known

00:18:39.280 --> 00:18:42.530
before I've met down, before
I came down here will come

00:18:42.530 --> 00:18:47.483
to me and ask me if I ate,
asked me if I need anything.

00:18:48.470 --> 00:18:49.770
It's a lot of people like that,

00:18:49.770 --> 00:18:52.280
you will meet on the streets
versus someone that's sitting

00:18:52.280 --> 00:18:53.913
at your table expecting a plate.

00:18:55.410 --> 00:18:56.560
You will find downtown.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.070
- [Interviewer] What are
you doing for money now?

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:04.210
- Right now I'm actually
just taking it day by day.

00:19:04.210 --> 00:19:06.660
If it comes, it comes, If
it doesn't, it doesn't.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:10.327
- [Interviewer] Are you
back to work in the streets

00:19:10.327 --> 00:19:11.223
dating guys?

00:19:12.070 --> 00:19:13.600
- No, because I'm pregnant.

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:16.800
Self-respect I couldn't do that.

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:19.370
Well, I serve every now and again.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:20.640
Yes I will.

00:19:20.640 --> 00:19:22.400
- [Interviewer] You
say serve meaning what?

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:23.440
- I was (indistinct)

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:25.360
- [Interviewer] Oh, I see.

00:19:25.360 --> 00:19:26.420
- If push come to the show

00:19:26.420 --> 00:19:28.000
but I receive everything that I need

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:32.290
without the value of a
dollar every day, every day.

00:19:32.290 --> 00:19:33.610
- [Interviewer] You get depressing times?

00:19:33.610 --> 00:19:34.965
- Yes I do.

00:19:34.965 --> 00:19:35.798
- [Interviewer] What
aspect of all this life

00:19:35.798 --> 00:19:39.027
gets you down the most?

00:19:39.027 --> 00:19:40.630
- The fact that all three of my children

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:41.830
are not with me anymore.

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:44.840
Like those were my shadows.

00:19:44.840 --> 00:19:47.470
I couldn't even go to the
bathroom without them.

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:51.890
So to look back and not hear
mom, at least a million times

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:56.640
in one sentence, it really
tears me up because like

00:19:56.640 --> 00:19:57.913
they are my everything.

00:19:59.705 --> 00:20:04.210
When I can't find a piece of
happiness, I can always look

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:07.303
at them and find it and know
that they won't judge me.

00:20:08.600 --> 00:20:12.610
I just wished that at one
point in time, I can actually

00:20:12.610 --> 00:20:14.693
have us all back in the same house.

00:20:15.650 --> 00:20:20.360
But if I can say something
to them, I will let them know

00:20:21.702 --> 00:20:25.433
that I'm trying hard to
get back to home every day.

00:20:26.385 --> 00:20:29.035
I try, it's a battle and it's hard

00:20:29.035 --> 00:20:32.343
because I miss him so much.

00:20:33.672 --> 00:20:35.203
I do like kids.

00:20:36.517 --> 00:20:39.310
They can get a bit irritating at times

00:20:39.310 --> 00:20:41.439
but that's just their job.

00:20:41.439 --> 00:20:45.470
But the moment that a
parent doesn't get to

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:50.470
enjoy that moment anymore,
or to hear your kids fighting

00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:54.000
or to see them riding
bikes or stuff like that

00:20:54.000 --> 00:20:59.000
it really hurts when you are a
rural parent, it hurts a lot.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.993
Like I don't get to roll
over and see my kids.

00:21:04.350 --> 00:21:08.110
I put them in their own beds
and wake up at 12 o'clock

00:21:08.110 --> 00:21:09.980
in the morning and see somebody laying

00:21:09.980 --> 00:21:12.083
on my neck or somebody by my foot.

00:21:13.045 --> 00:21:14.363
Like, it's really hard.

00:21:15.690 --> 00:21:16.523
And it hurts.

00:21:18.417 --> 00:21:20.760
- [Interviewer] And you
lost them for what reason?

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:23.483
- I couldn't take care of them anymore.

00:21:25.112 --> 00:21:28.330
I had no place for us to live.

00:21:28.330 --> 00:21:32.573
And me as a parent, I couldn't
take my kids through that.

00:21:34.190 --> 00:21:35.890
Me, I'm not stable myself.

00:21:35.890 --> 00:21:38.310
I didn't want my kids to go through this.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:40.990
Living in tents, running the
streets, doing all that stuff.

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:43.570
A lot of people would say
I gave up, but I didn't.

00:21:43.570 --> 00:21:45.030
I just seem better for my kids.

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:48.260
And it wasn't with me at this moment.

00:21:48.260 --> 00:21:50.580
So I let them live with their dad.

00:21:50.580 --> 00:21:53.090
I still have access to
phone calls, visits.

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:56.183
They just physically don't
live in a home with me anymore.

00:21:59.101 --> 00:22:02.840
And every day I wake up,
I pray and I fight hard.

00:22:04.120 --> 00:22:08.070
Whatever it is I need to
do to get back to them.

00:22:08.070 --> 00:22:12.973
I'm trying to do, anything.

00:22:15.820 --> 00:22:19.110
No child deserves to grow
up without their parents.

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:24.110
I grew up without mine
and it gives you questions

00:22:24.350 --> 00:22:27.120
that no child should ever question.

00:22:27.120 --> 00:22:28.633
Does my mom love me?

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:31.590
Was I not good enough?

00:22:31.590 --> 00:22:33.840
I don't ever want my
kids to experience that.

00:22:34.970 --> 00:22:36.593
Never, 'cause I did as a kid.

00:22:37.520 --> 00:22:40.470
Waking up in the middle of the
night and not seeing my mom.

00:22:41.730 --> 00:22:43.403
I want to break the cycle.

00:22:45.100 --> 00:22:47.443
I want to be the mom that came back.

00:22:52.300 --> 00:22:53.390
- [Interviewer] Okay, thank you so much

00:22:53.390 --> 00:22:54.360
for sharing your story.

00:22:54.360 --> 00:22:55.193
- No problem.

00:22:56.126 --> 00:22:57.300
- [Interviewer] I hope
you get your kids back.

00:22:57.300 --> 00:22:59.856
- I hope so too, thank you.

00:22:59.856 --> 00:23:02.023
- [Interviewer] Thank you.

